# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use TEM, a quantum function by Algorithmiq, to recover the dynamics of a 31-qubit kicked Ising chain from noisy hardware data, and compare it with PEC and ZNE."
msgstr "Gamitin ang TEM, isang quantum function ng Algorithmiq, para mabawi ang dynamics ng 31-qubit na kicked Ising chain mula sa noisy na hardware data, at ihambing ito sa PEC at ZNE."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a kicked Ising model with the TEM function"
msgstr "Simulate ang isang kicked Ising model gamit ang TEM function"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles, informationally */}\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithmiq's Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that removes the effect of hardware noise entirely in classical post-processing. The circuit runs on the QPU as written, with an informationally complete (IC) measurement at the end. A tensor network that inverts the learned noise of the device is then applied to the measurement outcomes, giving error-mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Ang Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method ng Algorithmiq ay isang hybrid quantum-classical algorithm na ganap na nag-aalis ng epekto ng hardware noise sa classical post-processing. Tumatakbo ang circuit sa QPU ayon sa pagkakasulat, na may informationally complete (IC) na measurement sa dulo. Ina-apply naman sa mga resulta ng measurement ang isang tensor network na nag-i-invert sa natutunang noise ng device, na nagbibigay ng mga error-mitigated na expectation value.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reproduces, at 31 qubits, the kind of many-body dynamics experiment run on up to 91 qubits in [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). It shows:\n"
msgstr "Ginagaya ng tutorial na ito, sa 31 qubit, ang uri ng many-body dynamics experiment na pinatakbo sa hanggang 91 qubit sa [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). Ipinapakita nito ang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much signal hardware noise destroys in a utility-scale dynamics circuit, and how much TEM recovers.\n"
msgstr "Gaano karaming signal ang sinisira ng hardware noise sa isang utility-scale na dynamics circuit, at gaano karami ang nababawi ng TEM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How TEM compares with probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) on the same circuit.\n"
msgstr "Paano maihahambing ang TEM sa probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) at zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) sa parehong circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IC measurement also makes it possible to estimate observables that were not requested when the circuit ran, with a rerun of only the classical post-processing. For an example that estimates the full light cone of a chain, see [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"
msgstr "Dahil sa IC measurement, posible ring tantiyahin ang mga observable na hindi hiniling noong tumakbo ang circuit, sa pamamagitan ng muling pagpapatakbo ng classical post-processing lang. Para sa halimbawang tumatantiya sa buong light cone ng isang chain, tingnan ang [Run 4: measure the light cone from the same data](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning#run-4-measure-the-light-cone-from-the-same-data).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To tune TEM's accuracy against its QPU and classical cost, see the companion example [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"
msgstr "Para i-tune ang katumpakan ng TEM laban sa QPU at classical na gastos nito, tingnan ang kasamang halimbawa na [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: approximately 20 QPU seconds for TEM on `ibm_phoenix` (the QPU time depends heavily on the chosen device). The optional PEC and ZNE comparison takes about 35 QPU minutes more, almost all of it for PEC.*\n"
msgstr "*Usage estimate: humigit-kumulang 20 QPU segundo para sa TEM sa `ibm_phoenix` (malaki ang nakadepende sa napiling device ang oras ng QPU). Ang opsyonal na paghahambing ng PEC at ZNE ay tumatagal ng humigit-kumulang 35 QPU minuto pa, halos lahat ay para sa PEC.*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background: the kicked Ising chain {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"
msgstr "Background: ang kicked Ising chain {#background-the-kicked-ising-chain}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The kicked Ising model alternates an Ising evolution on a chain of $N$ qubits,\n"
msgstr "Ang kicked Ising model ay nagsasalitan ng Ising evolution sa isang chain ng $N$ qubit,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n , $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a transverse kick,\n"
msgstr "na may transverse kick,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n . $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One period of the dynamics is the Floquet unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. On a quantum computer each period is a brickwork of two-qubit $ZZ$ rotations followed by single-qubit rotations, so the circuit contains only two distinct layers of two-qubit gates, repeated.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang period ng dynamics ay ang Floquet unitary na $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. Sa isang quantum computer, ang bawat period ay isang brickwork ng mga two-qubit $ZZ$ rotation na sinusundan ng mga single-qubit rotation, kaya dalawang natatanging layer lang ng mga two-qubit gate ang laman ng circuit, na inuulit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity of interest is the infinite-temperature autocorrelation function of the first spin. The [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) shows that it can be measured by preparing the first qubit in $|+\\rangle$ and every other pair of qubits in the Bell state $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, evolving for $t$ periods, and measuring a single-qubit Pauli operator $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"
msgstr "Ang quantity na pinag-uukulan ay ang infinite-temperature autocorrelation function ng unang spin. Ipinapakita ng [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) na maaari itong sukatin sa pamamagitan ng paghahanda sa unang qubit sa $|+\\rangle$ at sa bawat iba pang pares ng qubit sa Bell state na $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, pag-evolve sa loob ng $t$ period, at pagsukat ng isang single-qubit Pauli operator na $\\hat{X}_n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the dual unitary point $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$ the model is exactly solvable:\n"
msgstr "Sa dual unitary point na $|J| = |b| = \\pi/4$, eksaktong solvable ang model:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The correlation travels along the chain at maximal speed, so after $t$ periods only qubit $n = t$ carries it and $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Naglalakbay ang correlation sa chain sa pinakamataas na bilis, kaya pagkatapos ng $t$ period, ang qubit na $n = t$ lang ang may dala nito at $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n \\neq t} \\rangle = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "On that qubit, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"
msgstr "Sa qubit na iyon, $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=t} \\rangle = [\\cos(2h)]^t$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These exact values make the model a sharp benchmark for error mitigation: the signal that reaches qubit $t$ has passed through every layer of the circuit, so it is exposed to all the noise of the device, yet its noiseless value is known. Away from the dual unitary point the same circuits become hard to simulate classically, which is where the paper uses TEM to go beyond exact methods.\n"
msgstr "Dahil sa mga eksaktong value na ito, magandang benchmark ang model para sa error mitigation: ang signal na umaabot sa qubit $t$ ay dumaan sa bawat layer ng circuit, kaya nalalantad ito sa lahat ng noise ng device, pero alam ang noiseless na value nito. Malayo sa dual unitary point, nagiging mahirap i-simulate nang classical ang parehong mga circuit, at doon ginagamit ng paper ang TEM para lampasan ang mga eksaktong method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEM works in three steps: it learns the noise of each distinct layer of two-qubit gates and the readout error, runs the circuit with an IC measurement, and finally applies the noise-inverting tensor network to the measurement outcomes on IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana ang TEM sa tatlong hakbang: natututunan nito ang noise ng bawat natatanging layer ng mga two-qubit gate at ang readout error, pinapatakbo ang circuit na may IC measurement, at sa huli ay ina-apply ang noise-inverting tensor network sa mga resulta ng measurement sa IBM Cloud&reg;.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a prerequisite, ensure that the necessary dependencies are installed.\n"
msgstr "Bilang prerequisite, tiyakin na naka-install ang mga kinakailangang dependency.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Build the circuit and the observables {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"
msgstr "Step 1: Buuin ang circuit at ang mga observable {#step-1-build-the-circuit-and-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses a circuit that implements the kicked Ising model described in the previous section. The circuit is prepared as follows. First, there is a state preparation phase, in which the first qubit is in the state $|+\\rangle$, while the others are in Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. This is followed by the brickwork structure that implements the unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. The number of physical time steps corresponds to $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"The following code builds the circuit used in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng circuit na nagpapatupad ng kicked Ising model na inilarawan sa nakaraang seksyon. Ang circuit ay inihanda tulad ng sumusunod. Una, may isang state preparation phase, kung saan ang unang qubit ay nasa estado $|+\\rangle$, habang ang iba ay nasa Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. Sinusundan ito ng brickwork structure na nagpapatupad ng unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. Ang bilang ng mga physical time steps ay katumbas ng $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"Binubuo ng sumusunod na code ang circuit na ginamit sa tutorial na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, build the observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. It is constructed as a simple Pauli string with the order matching the one used by Qiskit:\n"
msgstr "Susunod, i-build ang observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. Ito ay itinayo bilang isang simpleng Pauli string na may order na tumutugma sa ginagamit ng Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment uses 31 qubits and 15 periods at $h = 0$, so the exact value of $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$ is 1. This is a utility-scale circuit with 465 two-qubit gates: 15 that prepare the Bell pairs and 30 in each period. The signal that reaches qubit 15 passes through hundreds of them.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang experiment ng 31 qubit at 15 period sa $h = 0$, kaya 1 ang eksaktong value ng $\\langle \\hat{X}_{n=15} \\rangle$. Isa itong utility-scale na circuit na may 465 two-qubit gate: 15 na naghahanda ng mga Bell pair at 30 sa bawat period. Ang signal na umaabot sa qubit 15 ay dumadaan sa daan-daan sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Run TEM on the QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Step 2: Patakbuhin ang TEM sa QPU {#step-2-run-tem-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, get access to the TEM function and select a backend from the available devices. This code assumes you've already [saved your account](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) to your local environment.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, kumuha ng access sa TEM function at pumili ng backend mula sa mga available na device. Ipinapalagay ng code na ito na [na-save mo na ang account mo](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) sa lokal mong environment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the TEM function from the [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"
msgstr "I-load ang TEM function mula sa [IBM Quantum&reg; Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit for the chosen device once, and map the observable onto the qubits it was placed on. TEM accepts this instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit as it is, and the PEC and ZNE comparison in Step 3 uses the same circuit, so all methods run the same gates on the same qubits.\n"
msgstr "I-transpile nang isang beses ang circuit para sa napiling device, at i-map ang observable sa mga qubit kung saan ito inilagay. Tinatanggap ng TEM ang instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit na ito nang ganito, at ginagamit ng paghahambing ng PEC at ZNE sa Step 3 ang parehong circuit, kaya pareho ang mga gate na pinapatakbo ng lahat ng method sa parehong mga qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following options are based on the physics of the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sumusunod na option ay batay sa physics ng circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: an upper bound on the number of distinct layers of two-qubit gates whose noise is learned. The brickwork has only two distinct layers, so only those two are learned.\n"
msgstr "**`max_layers_to_learn: 4`**: ang pinakamataas na limitasyon sa bilang ng magkakaibang layer ng two-qubit gates na ang noise ay pag-aaralan. Dalawa lang ang magkakaibang layer ng brickwork, kaya ang dalawang iyon lang ang natututunan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: the number of shots of the IC measurement, which sets the statistical precision of the estimate.\n"
msgstr "**`default_shots: 100_000`**: ang bilang ng shots ng IC measurement, na nagtatakda ng statistical precision ng estimate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** and **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: a moderate bond dimension that keeps the classical post-processing fast at 31 qubits, with a small cutoff so that the bond dimension is not truncated further.\n"
msgstr "**`tem_max_bond_dimension: 128`** at **`tem_compression_cutoff: 1e-14`**: isang katamtamang bond dimension na nagpapabilis sa classical post-processing sa 31 qubits, na may maliit na cutoff para hindi na ma-truncate pa ang bond dimension.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`private: False`**: keeps the job results downloadable later. Set it to `True` for confidential circuits.\n"
msgstr "**`private: False`**: pinapanatiling made-download ang mga resulta ng job sa ibang pagkakataon. Itakda ito sa `True` para sa mga confidential na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) explains each of these options in detail.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag nang detalyado ng [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) ang bawat isa sa mga option na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size that the job needs with the size calculator provided by IBM&reg;, and pass it to `tem.run` as `function_size`. The calculator maps the circuit onto the backend and returns `S`, `M`, or `L` without submitting anything; see [Function sizes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang function size na kailangan ng job gamit ang size calculator na ibinigay ng IBM&reg;, at ipasa ito sa `tem.run` bilang `function_size`. Ima-map ng calculator ang circuit sa backend at magbabalik ng `S`, `M`, o `L` nang hindi nagsa-submit ng kahit ano; tingnan ang [Function sizes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/get-started#function-sizes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, run the experiment, get the result, and visualize it. This step takes approximately 20 QPU seconds on `ibm_phoenix`.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, patakbuhin ang eksperimento, kunin ang resulta, at i-visualize ito. Ang hakbang na ito ay tumatagal ng humigit-kumulang 20 QPU seconds sa `ibm_phoenix`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save the job ID. Use it to retrieve the results later with `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, or to rerun the post-processing.\n"
msgstr "I-save ang job ID. Gamitin ito para kunin ang mga resulta sa ibang pagkakataon gamit ang `catalog.get_job_by_id(job_id)`, o para patakbuhing muli ang post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Compare with PEC and ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Ihambing sa PEC at ZNE {#step-3-compare-with-pec-and-zne}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result metadata also contains the unmitigated estimate, computed from the same measurement outcomes without the noise-inverting network. A comparison of the two with the exact value shows how much of the signal the noise destroys, and how much TEM recovers:\n"
"To put the TEM result in context, run the same circuit with two other error mitigation methods: probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with probabilistic error amplification (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The following code runs a large PEC experiment, which requires around 40 minutes of QPU time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Naglalaman din ang result metadata ng unmitigated estimate, na kinalkula mula sa parehong measurement outcomes nang walang noise-inverting network. Ipinapakita ng paghahambing ng dalawa sa exact value kung gaano karami sa signal ang sinisira ng noise, at kung gaano karami ang naibabalik ng TEM:\n"
"Para maunawaan ang konteksto ng resulta ng TEM, patakbuhin ang parehong circuit gamit ang dalawa pang error mitigation method: probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) at zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) na may probabilistic error amplification (PEA).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Ang sumusunod na code ay nagpapatakbo ng malaking PEC experiment, na nangangailangan ng humigit-kumulang 40 minuto ng QPU time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Note:** Each mitigation method can produce expectation values that are either higher or lower than the exact result. The standard deviations reflect statistical uncertainty only; they do not account for inaccuracies in the characterized noise model, because that model has no associated error bound.\n"
msgstr "> **Paalala:** Ang bawat mitigation method ay maaaring magbigay ng expectation values na mas mataas o mas mababa sa exact na resulta. Ang mga standard deviation ay sumasalamin lamang sa statistical uncertainty; hindi nila isinasaalang-alang ang mga kamalian sa characterized noise model, dahil walang kaugnay na error bound ang modelong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unmitigated value decays with the number of noisy gates in the light cone of qubit 15, so at this depth most of the signal is lost. TEM removes this decay in post-processing, recovering most of the signal without running any additional circuits. The remaining gap to the exact value comes from the speed-oriented settings used in this tutorial: a bond dimension of 128 and a modest noise-learning budget. The [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) shows how to trade QPU and classical time for accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Bumababa ang unmitigated value habang dumarami ang noisy gates sa light cone ng qubit 15, kaya sa lalim na ito ay karamihan ng signal ay nawawala. Inaalis ng TEM ang pagbaba na ito sa post-processing, at naibabalik ang karamihan ng signal nang hindi nagpapatakbo ng anumang karagdagang circuit. Ang natitirang agwat sa exact value ay galing sa mga setting na nakatuon sa bilis na ginamit sa tutorial na ito: bond dimension na 128 at katamtamang noise-learning budget. Ipinapakita ng [performance tuning example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning) kung paano ipagpalit ang QPU at classical time para sa accuracy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change $h$ in the circuit to move away from the exact value $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, or away from the dual unitary point, where classical simulation becomes hard. See [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) for results up to 91 qubits.\n"
msgstr "Baguhin ang $h$ sa circuit para lumayo sa exact value na $[\\cos(2h)]^t = 1$, o lumayo sa dual unitary point, kung saan nagiging mahirap ang classical simulation. Tingnan ang [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) para sa mga resulta hanggang 91 qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn how each TEM option affects accuracy, QPU time, and classical time in [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"
msgstr "Alamin kung paano nakakaapekto ang bawat TEM option sa accuracy, QPU time, at classical time sa [Tune the TEM function for accuracy and cost](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/performance-tuning).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the full list of options in the [TEM API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference).\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang buong listahan ng mga option sa [TEM API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<TutorialFeedback />\n"
msgstr "<TutorialFeedback />\n"
